---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import { GAME_IMAGES } from '../lib/images';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'About', path: '/about/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Main Sequence Guide"
  description="Main Sequence Guide is an independent, source-first wiki and tool site for the space factory sim. Learn our editorial approach, independence and image credits."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  pageType="AboutPage"
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="About the project"
    title="An independent field manual for Main Sequence"
    description="Main Sequence Guide is a fan-operated editorial project about the space factory sim, built to be useful before launch without pretending the game is finished."
    breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
    image={GAME_IMAGES['main-sequence-station-asteroid-belt.jpg']}
    imageAlt="A large Main Sequence station surrounded by asteroids"
    imageCaption="Official game imagery is used for editorial illustration. Site design and written analysis are original."
    meta={['Independent', 'Unofficial', 'Source-first']}
  />

  <div class="wrap py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_19rem]">
      <div class="prose-guide max-w-none">
        <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
        <p>
          Main Sequence is a game about turning a single mining ship into an
          industrial network. The information around it is scattered across a
          store page, developer announcements, patch notes, demo builds,
          community threads and videos. Our job is to collect the verifiable
          parts, explain the game in plain English and mark the blanks.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site is not affiliated with Tumbling Dumpling Studio, Mythwright
          or Valve. It is not an official wiki, and it does not speak for the
          developer. It is also not a review: we do not claim to have completed
          a build that is not public.
        </p>

        <h2>What we prioritize</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Accuracy over speed.</strong> When a detail is unconfirmed,
            the page says so. We do not turn an estimate into a fact to fill a
            table.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Useful pages over page count.</strong> A missing character
            database is better than invented characters. A missing recipe list
            is better than an invented calculator.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Independence.</strong> No developer payment changes a
            verdict, a label or a recommendation. Advertising, when enabled, is
            separated from editorial content.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Maintenance.</strong> The demo and launch build will change.
            Pages carry a last-checked date, and the update log is tied to
            official sources.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How the content is made</h2>
        <p>
          We use a combination of manual research, source comparison and
          AI-assisted drafting. The drafting process helps organize large
          amounts of public information; it is not treated as a source. Claims
          are checked against the links in each page’s source log. Any
          first-hand play impression or community-tested finding is labelled as
          such.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not claim to have playtested a build we have not played. Where a
          step comes from a community report—for example, the station-power
          workaround in the demo—the page explicitly marks it as
          community-tested and links to the report.
        </p>

        <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
        <p>
          Any future advertising is technical infrastructure, not editorial
          direction. Ad placements are labelled, and they do not influence
          source selection or page conclusions. If the site adds an affiliate
          link, it will be disclosed. We do not accept payment for a positive
          review or a guaranteed placement.
        </p>

        <h2>Images and trademarks</h2>
        <p>
          Screenshots are official Steam/press media, copyright Tumbling
          Dumpling Studio and Mythwright, used for editorial commentary and
          illustration. The site does <em>not</em> use the official game logo as
          its own mark; the field-guide mark, layouts, charts and written
          material are original to this project.
        </p>

        <h2>What comes next</h2>
        <p>
          After the Early Access build is public, the priorities are to verify
          the launch state, rebuild the database from stable in-game data, and
          add pages only where the game provides real entities: ships, modules,
          resources, locations or systems. We will not publish empty route
          variants to chase keywords.
        </p>

        <div class="callout callout-info">
          <span class="callout-title">Corrections welcome</span>
          <p class="m-0">
            If a source link is wrong, a mechanic changed, or a detail is
            mislabelled, send the page URL and a verifiable source to{' '}
            <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
            Corrections are more important than defending a draft.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside>
        <div class="sticky top-28 border border-line-soft bg-night p-5">
          <p class="font-mono text-[0.58rem] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-signal">
            Site record
          </p>
          <dl class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
            <div>
              <dt class="font-mono text-[0.55rem] uppercase tracking-[0.06em] text-mist">Project</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-fog">Unofficial fan resource</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="font-mono text-[0.55rem] uppercase tracking-[0.06em] text-mist">Focus</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-fog">Main Sequence wiki, guides and tools</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="font-mono text-[0.55rem] uppercase tracking-[0.06em] text-mist">Contact</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 break-all text-fog">{SITE.contactEmail}</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="font-mono text-[0.55rem] uppercase tracking-[0.06em] text-mist">Last checked</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-fog">{SITE.lastVerifiedLabel}</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <a href="/editorial-policy/" class="arrow-link mt-5">Editorial policy</a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
